 "_": "Objs named cert_<something> that are not certificates. The unpacker names an obj after whatever sits at the previous id, so the obj one past a law talisman is called cert_law_talisman while really being a Rotten net.",
 "why": "tools/pack/config/ObjConfig.ts writes the forward note link by looking up cert_<debugname>, and used to write it whether or not the other end was a note - so withdrawing a law talisman as a note handed over the Rotten net. The packer now requires certtemplate on the other end, and these are the objs that therefore no longer link. They are listed rather than counted so that a REAL note losing its certtemplate cannot hide among them: tools/certcheck.py fails if this set changes.",
 "renaming": "None of them is referenced by any script, config or map, so they could be renamed to something truthful - which would also stop tools/obtainable.py hiding them behind its ^cert_ rule. Not done: it is 132 renames in a generated file and a separate decision.",
